2026-10-28T17:32:55.4467533Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NMynKMtDjh3c2GFzCfZ6Z8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 20,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/20\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"Iceberg tables created with binary column using terraform is showing as unknown (type: varbyte) in Glue catalog\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```console\\nterraform --version\\nTerraform v1.15.5\\non darwin_arm64\\n+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/aws v6.49.0\\n+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/random v3.9.0\\n+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/time v0.14.0\\n+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/tls v4.3.0\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n* `aws_glue_catalog_table`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nGlue catalog should show binary column as binary type in glue catalog and binary in Athena Console\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nGlue catalog is showing as unknown column type (varbyte) in glue catalog and varbyte in Athena Console\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output\\n\\n```console\\n\\n```\\n\\n\\n### Sample Terraform Configuration\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand configuration</summary>\\n\\n```hcl\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Create iceberg table having column with binary datatype using terraform aws provider latest version\\n2. check the  Glue catalog UI for that table (unknown type - click on that link - you will see type:varbyte)\\n3.  check the table in Athena Console left drop down (you will see varbyte)\\n\\n### Debug Logging\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand log output</summary>\\n\\n```console\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### GenAI / LLM Assisted Development\\n\\nn/a\\n\\n### Important Facts and References\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\